Z||000000||BellaFiero||07-19-2000||02:51 PM||||Hey Folks! Maybe one of you can help me out here... my fiance's brother has a 1987 Mustang LX. He wants to do the whole racing thing. Now, I know I have him beat. A four cylinder Fiero with the mods and customized shenanigans that make the Bella Donna can eat four-banging Mustangs for breakfast. But - his Mustang has glass packs on it's exhaust and it sounds AWESOME. How hard would it be to do with a Fiero? I'm running a four cylinder engine with a 88 GT's exhaust.. is it merely bolting the pack onto the bottom of the car and running pipes from one end to the other, or what? How exactly, and what exactly, are they? I've restored alot of old muscle cars, but I've never really been interested in sound over performance. But with a four banger... can you guys help me? Send me down that shining path? Let me know!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>"No! NO! You can't put that there! There won't be enough room for the Johnson Rod then! What are you thinkin'?!?"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||07-19-2000||03:45 PM||||<BR>As the proud owner of a 4-banger Fiero myself, I have to say I doubt that ANY four cylinder engine could sound <I>awesome</I> ...compared to a V8 with a lumpy bumpstick anyway. However, different strokes for different folks. One thing that caught my attention in your post Bella was that you mentioned this 4-banger Mustang has "glass pack<I>s</I>", as in more than one. How is this acomplished, or is that simply a spelling error? Even I might be interested in a true dual-exhaust with glass packs on my Fiero. Would bring back fond memories of the ol' 396... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||ChadMan||07-19-2000||04:10 PM||||My 88 Coupe's cat was clogged, so it somehow got replaced with a Thrush "cherry bomb" muffler that the parts-store guy referred to as a "glass pack".  (Can't say I replaced it since that's a federal enviro-Nazi-crime.)  It leaks a little where I...er...someone did a lousy job with the muffler putty.<P>It has a nice blatty exhaust note that sounds healthier than an MGB or Spitfire, but not quite as cool as a 944.  It's not buzzy or farty like a ricer - 2.5 liters is too big for that.<P>Now if only I could do something about that clattery John Deere idle sound...||||reg||7
Z||000003||tgowens||07-19-2000||07:54 PM||||"glass-packs" -- I hadn't heard that term for a long time!! I can remember putting two glass-packs on my '65 GTO and running til they were hot then sticking a garden hose up the tailpipe and hitting the glass with cold water - then "blowing them out" -- ahhhhh, those were the good ol' days! - of course, I had a GTO with a 389 tri=power too!||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||07-20-2000||01:27 AM||||Good Post Bella....This was mentioned here a while back.. I plan on doing a TRUE DUAL  ex. on my 87GT.... someone on here said that it sound's like a v-10????  i dont know.. But I think I'm going to try it anyhow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>                             Steve '87GT<BR>                                   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||BellaFiero||07-20-2000||09:15 AM||||Let me know how it goes... I'm going to the many auto stores and see what I can come up with. Dual exhaust would be excellent... I'm going to see what it takes to mount one of these packs.||||reg||10
Z||000006||stsmithgt||07-20-2000||09:37 AM||||Ah the snap crackle pop of glass packs.  What a memory.  I had some 16" ones behind a big block 390 in a 68 galaxy fastback.  What a beast.  The exhaust would scare the rivals right off the starting line with their tails between their legs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">  ||||reg||10
Z||000007||Formula||07-20-2000||01:21 PM||||1Fiero.......If your GT sounds like a V-10 when your done then I want some part numbers!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!hey whats that car. It must be one of those Fiero V-10s....<P>pulling up next to a viper.......REV.... HEY WHY DOES YOUR CAR SOUND LIKE MINE..... isnt that what a V-10 sounds like???? <P>I could only dream ||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||07-20-2000||03:56 PM||||Any small independently owned muffler shop will be happy to take your money and cut off your nice quiet Fiero muffler and weld on a loud crappy glasspack in it's place. My Dad used to refer to them as "cop callers" and boy, was he right. I had them on my 68 Chevelle SS 396 for a while until I got tired of getting pulled over all the time. I switched to turbo mufflers (we didn't have Flowmasters back then) and everything was much better at no sacrifice to performance. Glasspacks are fiberglass packed and the "glass" burns out fairly quickly leaving you with a very loud car. Just what some people like, but watch out for the cops and annoyed neighbors.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BellaFiero||07-21-2000||10:02 AM||||Well, they're certainly loud on his 'Stang, but it's got a nice rumble too it. And I don't have to worry about neighbors - I work on their cars  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> The guy next door, Larry, owns a Dodge Ram that we've tricked out to infinity and beyond. I live out in the country - but ten minutes from the closest mall ( go figure - but hey, I love it. ) As far as cops go, there's the interior neon kit, the scanner-light, and the thundering bass - why not exhaust noise? Actually, the cops all know my car and we get into pretty heated discussions while we sit at Denny's and argue over politics  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So I'm not worried about either of those. But what I do want it to somehow keep the exhaust "appearing" stock... at the least the four tips...  Fairview Heights - in the middle of nowhere and ten minutes from everywhere.||||reg||12
Z||000010||Patrick||07-21-2000||12:51 PM||||<BR>Bella, I'm still curious. In reference to the glass pack<I>s</I> on your friend's car, you stated, "<I>they're</I> certainly loud..." Could you please let us know how a 4-banger Mustang manages to have more than one muffler. If it's simply ONE exhaust pipe split into TWO tailpipes (and two mufflers), what's the point?<p>[This message has been edited by Patrick (edited 07-21-2000).]||||reg||5
